# Feature & Module Structure (Mandatory)

PharmaConnect uses **two** code homes. Pick one before adding code:

| Location | Use when |
|----------|----------|
| `src/features/<featureName>/` | Route-level pages, auth, onboarding flows, settings tabs — **orchestration** tied to a route or product area |
| `src/shared/modules/<DomainModule>/` | Reusable domain UI + data (tables, modals, filters, services) consumed by **2+ features** or admin + pharmacist surfaces |

**Examples:** `features/inventory` owns the route page; `shared/modules/InventoryModule` owns `InventoryTable`, hooks, and services. `features/Settings/.../PharmacistsTab` imports `PharmacistsSettingsModule` from `PharmacistsModule`.

### Component nesting (max one level)

- **One parent → one level of children only** — no `components/X/components/Y`
- Child components are **sibling `.tsx` files** in the parent folder, or one purpose subfolder (`fields/`, `columns/`) — not another `components/` tree
- If a child needs its own children → extract a new top-level component file or move to `src/components/ui/`

```
✅ components/RefundModal/RefundModal.tsx + RefundModal/CustomerDetails.tsx
✅ modals/AddEditModal/fields/NameField.tsx
❌ components/Tab/components/Section/components/Row.tsx
```

---

## `src/features/<featureName>/`

```
src/features/<featureName>/
├── components/          ← UI scoped to this feature/route (`<name>.component.tsx` + `index.ts`)
├── hooks/               ← React Query hooks scoped to this feature
├── types/               ← UI-only types (`<name>.types.ts` + `index.ts` barrel)
├── schemas/             ← Zod validation (forms, API boundaries)
├── pages/               ← route-level page components (lazy-loaded)
├── services/            ← only when API calls are feature-specific
└── index.ts             ← public surface (do NOT export pages)
```

**Minimum required:** `components/`, `hooks/`, `index.ts`.
Add `types/`, `schemas/`, `pages/`, `services/` only when needed — no empty folders.

### Feature rules

- **Never scatter feature code** — all code lives inside `src/features/<featureName>/`
- **`index.ts` is the only public surface** — `import from "@/features/<featureName>"`, never deep paths
- **Delegate domain tables/modals** to `src/shared/modules/` when the same UI appears in multiple places
- **Shared UI** (2+ features, not domain-specific) → `src/components/ui/`
- **Page components** live in `pages/` and are lazy-loaded from the router
- **`index.ts` must not export page components** — router imports pages directly

---

## `src/shared/modules/<DomainModule>/`

Folder name: **`PascalCase` + `Module`** — `InventoryModule`, `PharmacistsModule`, `OrdersModule`.

```
src/shared/modules/<DomainModule>/
├── components/          ← tables, filters, settings shells (`<name>.component.tsx` + `index.ts`)
├── hooks/               ← orchestration hooks (`use<Domain>Table`, modals, forms)
│   ├── queries/       ← `useQuery` / `useInfiniteQuery` only
│   └── mutations/     ← `useMutation` only
├── services/            ← API calls (*.service.ts) + services/index.ts barrel
├── columns/             ← table column definitions
├── modals/              ← add/edit/detail modal flows
├── constants/           ← filters, initial state, table config
├── types/               ← module-local UI types (`<name>.types.ts` + `index.ts`)
├── utils/               ← query-param builders, export helpers — **not** response mappers
├── schema.ts            ← Zod schemas (when module has forms) — optional
└── index.ts             ← ONLY public surface
```

**Minimum required:** `components/`, `hooks/`, `services/`, `index.ts`.
Add `columns/`, `modals/`, `constants/`, `types/`, `utils/`, `schema.ts` only when needed.

### Module rules

- **One module = one domain** — inventory, orders, pharmacists, branches, customers, refunds
- **`index.ts` is the only public surface** — `import from "@/shared/modules/<DomainModule>"`
- **Co-locate services inside the module** — not `src/services/` (legacy `src/services/` is not used for these domains)
- **Queries live in** `hooks/queries/` — `useQuery` / `useInfiniteQuery` only (e.g. `useBranchList.ts`, `useCustomerOrders.ts`)
- **Mutations live in** `hooks/mutations/` — `useMutation` only (e.g. `useAddBranch.ts`, `useBranchLinkWithMeta.ts`)
- **Orchestration hooks stay in** `hooks/` root — `use<Domain>Table.ts` (state + infinity `fetchFn`), `use<Domain>Modals.ts`, form wiring
- **All API logic lives in** `services/` — one file per action (`getOrders.service.ts`, `getOrdersByRole.service.ts`, `fetchOrdersPage.service.ts`)
- **Hooks are thin** — React Query wiring only (`queryKey`, `queryFn`, `enabled`, `staleTime`); **never** inline `fetch*` helpers or `Api` calls in hooks
- **Use backend DTOs in UI** — import types from `@/shared/types/dtos/`; **no mapper utils** unless the API shape truly differs (prefer backend fixes or column-level display)
- **Role branching** (admin vs pharmacist) → dedicated `*ByRole.service.ts` that calls the low-level endpoint services
- **Infinity-table pagination** → `fetch<Domain>Page.service.ts` adapts API response to `{ data, meta }` for the table
- **Table columns** → single `columns/<domain>Columns.tsx` with `use<Domain>TableColumns`; inline column objects in `useMemo` (no split column files, no `buildColumns` helpers)
- **`constants/`** → `initialFilters.ts` (default filter state) + `filters.ts` (e.g. `use<Domain>FilterItems` hook)
- **Module `types/`** → UI-only shapes (filters, service params); **API row types** come from `@/shared/types/dtos/` — do not duplicate DTOs in the module
- **Cross-module hooks** → if a hook serves 2+ modules (e.g. city search), place in `src/shared/hooks/` — not inside one module
- **Complex flows live in** `modals/<Name>/` with optional `fields/` subfolder — **no** `modals/<Name>/components/<Child>/components/`
- **Modules may import other modules** through their `index.ts` only — e.g. `PharmacistsModule` imports `useBranches` from `BranchesModule`
- **Features import modules, not the other way around** — modules must not import from `src/features/`

### Hook responsibilities (table modules)

| Hook | Location | Responsibility |
|------|----------|----------------|
| `use<Domain>Table.ts` | `hooks/` | Orchestration: modal state, `querySignature`, `useCallback` fetch fn → `fetch<Domain>Page.service.ts` |
| `use<Domain><Resource>.ts` | `hooks/queries/` | Single `useQuery` / `useInfiniteQuery` — `queryFn` calls a service only |
| `use<Domain><Action>.ts` | `hooks/mutations/` | Single `useMutation` — calls a service only |

### Service layers (table + role-scoped APIs)

```
getCustomers.service.ts           ← raw Api GET (admin + pharmacist endpoints)
getCustomerOrdersByRole.service.ts ← picks endpoint by role; unwraps StandardApiResponse
fetchCustomersPage.service.ts     ← maps list API to { data, meta } for infinity scroll table
```

